=> Now test multiple Linux commands

Change your program to:

import subprocess

def run_command(command):
    result = subprocess.run(
        command,
        capture_output=True,
        text=True
    )

    return result.stdout


print("Hostname:")
print(run_command(["hostname"]))

print("Uptime:")
print(run_command(["uptime"]))

print("Memory:")
print(run_command(["free", "-h"]))

print("Disk:")
print(run_command(["df", "-h", "/"]))

Run:
python3 function_test.py

Now one function is handling four different Linux commands.

That's much better.
